# Frontend Standards

- Use Vue 3 Composition API with `<script setup lang="ts">`.
- Use strict TypeScript, typed props/emits, and avoid `any`.
- Follow existing project architecture and conventions.
- Prefer modern native CSS over unnecessary JavaScript or UI dependencies.
- Use CSS Grid, Flexbox, custom properties, clamp(), and container queries where appropriate.
- Build responsive layouts intentionally, not as an afterthought.
- Use semantic HTML and accessible interactive elements.
- Respect keyboard navigation, focus states, contrast, and reduced-motion preferences.
- Extract reusable components based on meaningful repetition.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions, oversized components, and excessive dependencies.
- Preserve established design tokens and visual patterns.
- For new UI work or visual redesigns, load the frontend-design skill before implementation.
